uv sync --locked
{% if profile == 'service' %}uv run uvicorn {{ packageName }}.app:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000{% elif profile == 'native' %}uv run python -c 'import {{ packageName }}; print({{ packageName }}.__name__)'{% else %}uv run python -c 'import {{ packageName }}; print({{ packageName }}.__name__)'{% endif %}
```

## 🧭 Architecture

`src/{{ packageName }}` owns the Python package.{% if profile == 'service' %} `app.py` composes the HTTP application and `settings.py` validates environment input. `/health/live` checks process response; `/health/ready` checks only enabled dependencies.{% if withPersistence | default(false) %} This render requires `DATABASE_URL` at startup and includes async PostgreSQL/Alembic wiring, but no domain schema or migration revision.{% else %} This render has no required database or credentials.{% endif %} Add business adapters only around actual requirements.{% elif profile == 'native' %} `native/` owns C++ behavior and `_core` stays private; the Python package is the public interface.{% endif %} Record project-specific decisions in [PROJECT.md](PROJECT.md){% if profile == 'service' %} and [SERVICE.md](SERVICE.md){% endif %}.

